Advantages and Disadvantages of this, hence what came next
==========================================================

Advantages
----------
1. Protects aggregated links.
2. Prevents unauthorized channel formation.
3. Improves redundancy.
4. Enhances availability.
5. Supports secure load balancing.
6. Improves STP stability.
7. Reduces link-related failures.

Disadvantages
-------------
1. Requires configuration consistency.
2. Troubleshooting can be complex.
3. Misconfigured members may be suspended.
4. Additional administrative effort.
5. Must be monitored regularly.

Hence what came next
--------------------
Even with secure EtherChannels, excessive Layer 2 traffic can still overwhelm the network.

Examples:

- Broadcast Storms
- Malware Outbreaks
- Switching Loops
- Faulty Devices

Administrators needed a way to limit excessive traffic.

This led to:

Storm Control

which limits Broadcast, Multicast, and Unknown Unicast traffic.

One-Shot Configuration
======================

Configure EtherChannel Using LACP

Switch(config)# interface range g0/1-2
Switch(config-if-range)# channel-group 1 mode active


Configure Port-Channel

Switch(config)# interface port-channel 1
Switch(config-if)# switchport mode trunk
Switch(config-if)# switchport trunk allowed vlan 10,20,30
Switch(config-if)# switchport nonegotiate


(Optional)

Enable UDLD on Member Links

Switch(config)# interface range g0/1-2
Switch(config-if-range)# udld port aggressive
====================================================

or 


interface range g0/1-2
 channel-group 1 mode active
 udld port aggressive

interface port-channel1
 switchport mode trunk
 switchport trunk allowed vlan 10,20,30
 switchport trunk native vlan 999
 switchport nonegotiate
 spanning-tree guard root


Verification
============

show etherchannel summary

show etherchannel port-channel

show interfaces port-channel 1

show lacp neighbor

